  "id": "Compound::DB00175 - Gene::3156",
  "verbalization": "Pravastatin's relationship with Hmgcr is mediated through Rosuvastatin, a known Hmg-Coa reductase inhibitor. The evidence suggests that Pravastatin causes muscle swelling and immune-mediated necrotising myopathy, both of which are linked to Rosuvastatin. Rosuvastatin, in turn, binds to Hmgcr, indicating a direct interaction between the two entities. The shared lowest common ancestor, Hydroxy monocarboxylic acid, further supports a common pathway in the metabolic regulation of Hmgcr. The consistent involvement of Rosuvastatin in both pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Pravastatin influences Hmgcr, likely through its effect on the metabolic cascade initiated by Rosuvastatin. This integrated evidence suggests that Pravastatin may modulate Hmgcr activity via its interaction with Rosuvastatin, emphasizing the role of Hmg-Coa reductase inhibitors in the broader context of lipid metabolism.",
